                                "sense_id": "1d8a457a-d86c-31c7-a8fc-263be3e40d99",
                                "text": "Between our human nature and the nature they desiderate there is a deep and fordless river, over which they can throw no bridge, and all their talk supposes that we shall be able to fly or wade across it […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62e6c0eb-e565-4788-b2a1-67966a544c6b",
                                "sense_id": "1d8a457a-d86c-31c7-a8fc-263be3e40d99",
                                "text": "2006, Maha-bhárata, Book 7, Volume 1, Clay Sanskrit Library, edited and translated by Vaughan Pilikian, New York University Press, p. 185,\nDrona poured forth a river of death. […] Not fish but swords swam in its fordless waters, and elephants and horses were where sharks might have been."
                            }
